.TH CRABWALLD 8 "September 2026" "crabwall 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
crabwalld \- per-app firewall daemon for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crabwalld
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crabwalld
watches outbound connections and enforces per-application firewall rules.
With privileges it steers TCP/UDP output into an NFQUEUE and holds each
new connection's first packet until the user answers (timeout denies).
Without privileges it falls back to nftables set enforcement and logs
decisions. Unknown connections are prompted through
.BR crabwall (1);
nothing unmatched is ever silently allowed under the default policy.
.PP
Sources of attribution, in order: eBPF connect feed (instant pid),
5-tuple correlator, on-demand /proc socket scan,
.B NFQA_UID
from queued packets, passive DNS/SNI sniffer, reverse DNS (opt-in).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRABWALL_DEFAULT
Default policy for unmatched traffic:
.B ask
(default),
.B allow
or
.B deny .
.TP
.B CRABWALL_PTR=1
Enable background reverse-DNS warming of the domain cache.
.TP
.B CRABWALL_LEARN_SECS=N
Learn mode: allow unknown traffic for N seconds and append suggestions
to
.I rules.suggested.toml
for review.
.TP
.B CRABWALL_SOCK , CRABWALL_RULES , CRABWALL_DB , CRABWALL_EBPF_OBJ
Override the socket, rules file, log database and eBPF object paths.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/crabwall.sock
Control socket (root service).
.TP
.I ~/.config/crabwall/rules.toml
Rules. Format:
.RS
.nf
[[rule]]
app = "firefox"              # basename or full /usr/bin/... path
domain_suffix = "google.com" # optional suffix match
ports = [80, 443]            # optional, empty = all
container = "abc123def456"   # optional Docker id
sandbox = "org.foo.Bar"      # optional Flatpak id / snap name
action = "deny"              # allow | deny | ask
.fi
.RE
Most constrained matching rule wins; otherwise the default applies.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/crabwall/events.db
SQLite log of all decisions (rotated at ~50k rows).
.SH PRIVILEGES
Needs root (or CAP_NET_ADMIN + CAP_SYS_RESOURCE + CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH)
for nftables, NFQUEUE, the packet sniffer and eBPF. Without them the
daemon runs in dry-run log-only mode.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Runs until terminated.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR crabwall (1),
.BR nft (8)
.SH AUTHORS
crabwall contributors.
